            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LEWIKE01"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As the writer of this recipe, I just want to point out some errors in the editing. 6 inches from the heat source is WAY too close and that's why people are getting burnt coconut! I'd say 12-15 inches, depending on your oven. Also, the vanilla ice cream is a key ingredient that got bumped into the description. It's not the same without it!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aliboo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nice easy sweet dessert, if you have problems with the coconut burning, best to put it in with just the brown sugar first, once it starts to bubble, add the coconut, doing it this way, you have control of how brown it gets. Be warned, coconut browns very quickly!",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-19T06:21:17.653Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lasara1983"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Had some crushed pineapple along with 2 slices of pineapple leftover from an upside down pineapple cake I made. I didn't want to throw it away so I found this instead. Anyways I did mine with a twist on the stove and added some butter and corn starch to thicken it. I kind of want to add some bread to it now and make it into something like a cobbler =)",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-02T13:10:35.123Z"
          },
          {
